IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- SCHEDULES 1, 2, 3 and 3AZA of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds
-- (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017, S.I. 2017/692, United Kingdom, lines 2956-3054 of
-- uksi-2017-692.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
-- Schedules 1 and 2 are the core's enumerations `Professional body` and `Listed activity`; the
-- functions here only ask membership of them.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  A decision function answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.
-- JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words; each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (...)` with the quoted words.  NOTHING is "the text does not answer"; each such
-- branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Marginal readings, listed in NOTES.md: (a) an "is"-definition or a closed list is the text's no;
-- (b) a grant limited by its own wording is not a no.
-- Rulings of 2026-11-05, tagged `[ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]` and `[ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]`
-- on the branch (they are not the marginal readings above): a period the text fixes in its own
-- words answers JUST FALSE outside it; a "where" condition that is not met answers JUST FALSE;
-- a scope limit with no "only" answers NOTHING outside the scope.
-- A duty function (a "must") answers JUST FALSE only for a breach.  Where the duty arises "if" or
-- "where" something holds, a companion function, `... the duty ... arises`, answers JUST FALSE when
-- it does not arise, and the duty function answers NOTHING then.
-- A seam is marked `-- SEAM S-n (asking|answering)`.

§ `Schedules`

§§ `Schedule 1 -- Professional bodies`

-- Schedule 1 lists twenty-two professional bodies.  They are the constructors of the core's type `Professional body` (lines 89-111 of mlr-core.l4); the text lines 2957-2978 are the table.  This function asks whether an Authority is one of them.
-- src:2956 | SCHEDULE 1 — Professional Bodies
-- src:2957 | Association of Accounting Technicians
-- src:2958 | Association of Chartered Certified Accountants
-- src:2959 | Association of International Accountants
-- src:2960 | Association of Taxation Technicians
-- src:2961 | Chartered Institute of Legal Executives
-- src:2962 | Chartered Institute of Management Accountants
-- src:2963 | Chartered Institute of Taxation
-- src:2964 | Council for Licensed Conveyancers
-- src:2965 | Faculty of Advocates
-- src:2966 | Faculty Office of the Archbishop of Canterbury
-- src:2967 | General Council of the Bar
-- src:2968 | General Council of the Bar of Northern Ireland
-- src:2969 | Insolvency Practitioners Association
-- src:2970 | Institute of Certified Bookkeepers
-- src:2971 | Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales
-- src:2972 | Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland
-- src:2973 | Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland
-- src:2974 | Institute of Financial Accountants
-- src:2975 | Institute of Accountants and Bookkeepers
-- src:2976 | Law Society
-- src:2977 | Law Society of Northern Ireland
-- src:2978 | Law Society of Scotland
@ref sch 1 (src:2956-2978)
GIVEN body IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 1 the body is a professional body listed in Schedule 1` IS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `a professional body listed in Schedule 1` listed THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Professional Bodies" listed in the Schedule; a body not among the twenty-two is not a "professional body listed in Schedule 1" [marginal (a)]

§§ `Schedule 2 -- Listed activities`

-- Schedule 2: the activities.  They are the constructors of the core's type `Listed activity`; the ten items that carry no condition of their own (2, 4, 5 and 7 to 13) are cited here and tested one by one; items 1, 3 and 6 follow with their own rules.  The sentence "The activities ... are—" closes the list.
-- src:2979 | SCHEDULE 2 — Listed Activities
-- src:2980 | The activities ... are—
-- src:2982 | Financial leasing.
-- src:2984 | Issuing and administering other means of payment (e.g. travellers' cheques and bankers' drafts) ....
-- src:2985 | Guarantees and commitments.
-- src:2992 | Participation in securities issues and the provision of services relating to such issues.
-- src:2993 | Advice to undertakings on capital structure, industrial strategy and related questions and advice as well as services relating to mergers and the purchase of undertakings.
-- src:2994 | Money broking.
-- src:2995 | Portfolio management and advice.
-- src:2996 | Safekeeping and administration of securities.
-- src:2997 | Safe custody services.
-- src:2998 | Issuing electronic money.
@ref sch 2 (src:2979-2980) (src:2982) (src:2984-2985) (src:2992-2998)
GIVEN `the activity, if it is one of the listed activities` IS A MAYBE `Listed activity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 2 the activity is a listed activity` IS
    CONSIDER `the activity, if it is one of the listed activities`
    WHEN JUST listed THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The activities ... are—" followed by the thirteen items [marginal (a)]

-- Schedule 2 item 1: "Lending including, inter alia" four examples; "inter alia" keeps the list open.
-- src:2981 | Lending including, inter alia: consumer credit, credit agreements relating to immovable property, factoring, with or without recourse, financing of commercial transactions (including forfeiting).
@ref sch 2 item 1 (src:2981)
GIVEN `the credit is consumer credit, a credit agreement relating to immovable property, factoring with or without recourse, or the financing of commercial transactions (including forfeiting)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 2 item 1 the kind of credit is within lending` IS
    IF `the credit is consumer credit, a credit agreement relating to immovable property, factoring with or without recourse, or the financing of commercial transactions (including forfeiting)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including, inter alia"

-- Schedule 2 item 3: payment services as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017, other than an account information service.
-- src:2983 | Payment services as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017, other than an account information service (within the meaning of that term in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations).
@ref sch 2 item 3 (src:2983)
GIVEN `the service is a payment service as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is an account information service (within the meaning of that term in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 2 item 3 the service is within payment services` IS
    IF `the service is a payment service as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017` AND (NOT `the service is an account information service (within the meaning of that term in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the service is a payment service as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017` AND (NOT `the service is an account information service (within the meaning of that term in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations)`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Payment services as defined in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017, other than an account information service" [marginal (a)]

-- Schedule 2 item 6: trading for own account or for the account of customers in any of five kinds of instrument.
-- src:2986 | Trading for own account or for account of customers in any of the following:
-- src:2987 | (a) money market instruments (cheques, bills, certificates of deposit, etc.);
-- src:2988 | (b) foreign exchange;
-- src:2989 | (c) financial futures and options;
-- src:2990 | (d) exchange and interest-rate instruments;
-- src:2991 | (e) transferable securities.
@ref sch 2 item 6 (src:2986-2991)
DECLARE `sch 2 item 6 instrument` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 item 6(a) money market instruments (cheques, bills, certificates of deposit, etc.)`
    `sch 2 item 6(b) foreign exchange`
    `sch 2 item 6(c) financial futures and options`
    `sch 2 item 6(d) exchange and interest-rate instruments`
    `sch 2 item 6(e) transferable securities`
    `sch 2 item 6 some other instrument`

@ref sch 2 item 6 (src:2986-2991)
GIVEN `the trading is for own account or for the account of customers` IS A BOOLEAN
      what IS A `sch 2 item 6 instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 2 item 6 the trading is within the item` IS
    IF `the trading is for own account or for the account of customers`
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `sch 2 item 6(a) money market instruments (cheques, bills, certificates of deposit, etc.)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `sch 2 item 6(b) foreign exchange` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `sch 2 item 6(c) financial futures and options` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `sch 2 item 6(d) exchange and interest-rate instruments` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `sch 2 item 6(e) transferable securities` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `sch 2 item 6 some other instrument` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any of the following" lists five kinds; the item does not say that trading in another kind is covered or excluded
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Trading for own account or for account of customers in any of the following"

§§ `Schedule 3 -- Relevant offences`

-- Schedule 3 lists thirty-six paragraphs in this rendering, which prints them without their numbers (fork F-SCH3-NUMBERS).  They are numbered here by position: the first line (3000) is paragraph 1 and the line "An act which—" (3035) is paragraph 36.  The text's own cross-reference in paragraph 36, "paragraphs 1 to 34" (line 3037), is consistent with that count: it reaches the last offence-specific paragraph before the two ancillary ones.  The offences themselves are described by the borrowed Acts, whose content is outside the sources, so the question put to this function is which paragraph the offence falls within.
-- src:3000 | An offence under the Perjury Act 1911 .
-- src:3001 | An offence under section 89 of the Criminal Justice Act 1967 (false written statements tendered in evidence) .
-- src:3002 | An offence under section 20BB of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (falsification of documents) .
-- src:3003 | An offence under section 11 of the European Communities Act 1972 (EU offences) .
-- src:3004 | An offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (false statutory declarations and other false unsworn statements) .
-- src:3005 | An offence under the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979 .
-- src:3006 | An offence under the Estate Agency Act 1979, or specified for the purposes of section 3 of that Act in the Estate Agents (Specified Offences) (No 2) Order 1991 .
-- src:3007 | An offence under any of sections 1 to 5 of the Forgery and Counterfeiting Act 1981 (counterfeiting offences).
-- src:3008 | An offence under section 35 of the Administration of Justice Act 1985 (penalty for pretending to be a licensed conveyancer or recognised body) .
-- src:3009 | An offence under section 11(1) (undischarged bankrupts) or 13 (criminal penalties) of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 .
-- src:3010 | An offence under section 1, 2, 3, 3ZA or 3A of the Computer Misuse Act 1990 (computer misuse offences).
-- src:3011 | An offence under section 112 (false representations or obtaining benefit) or 114 (offences relating to contributions) of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 .
-- src:3012 | An offence under section 52 of the Criminal Justice Act 1993 (the offence of insider dealing).
-- src:3013 | An offence under the Value Added Tax Act 1994 .
-- src:3014 | An offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995 (false statement and declarations) .
-- src:3015 | An offence under the Data Protection Act 1998 .
-- src:3016 | An offence under the Terrorism Act 2000 .
-- src:3017 | An offence under paragraph 7(2) or (3) of Schedule 3 to the Anti-Terrorism, Crime and Security Act 2001 (offences).
-- src:3018 | An offence under the Money Laundering Regulations 2001 , the Money Laundering Regulations 2003 , the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 or under these Regulations.
-- src:3019 | An offence under section 35 of the Tax Credits Act 2002 (offence of fraud).
-- src:3020 | An offence under Part 7 (money laundering) or Part 8 (investigations) of, or listed in Schedule 2 (lifestyle offences: England and Wales), 4 (lifestyle offences: Scotland) or 5 (lifestyle offences: Northern Ireland) to, the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 .
-- src:3021 | An offence under the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005 .
-- src:3022 | An offence under the Terrorism Act 2006 .
-- src:3023 | An offence under section 1, 2, 6 or 7 of the Bribery Act 2010 (bribery).
-- src:3024 | An offence under section 45 of the Serious Crime Act 2015 (offence of participating in activities of organised crime gang).
-- src:3025 | An offence under Parts 1 (general privacy protections); 2 (lawful interception of communications), 3 (authorisations for obtaining communications data), 5 (equipment interference), 6 (bulk warrants) and 7 (bulk personal dataset warrants) of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016 .
-- src:3026 | An offence under section 45 (failure to prevent facilitation of UK tax evasion offences) or 46 (failure to prevent facilitation of foreign tax evasion offences) of the Criminal Finances Act 2017 .
-- src:3027 | An offence under the Data Protection Act 2018, apart from an offence under section 173 of that Act.
-- src:3028 | An offence of cheating the public revenue.
-- src:3029 | An offence under the law of any part of the United Kingdom consisting of being knowingly concerned in, or in taking steps with a view to, the fraudulent evasion of tax.
-- src:3030 | Any offence which has deception or dishonesty as one of its components.
-- src:3031 | The common law offences of conspiracy to defraud and perverting the course of justice.
-- src:3032 | An offence of attempting, conspiring or inciting the commission of an offence specified in this Schedule.
-- src:3033 | An offence under section 44 of the Serious Crime Act 2007 of doing an act capable of encouraging or assisting the commission of an offence specified in this Schedule.
-- src:3034 | An offence of aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring the commission of an offence specified in this Schedule.
@ref sch 3 (src:3000-3034)
DECLARE `sch 3 paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `sch 3 para 1 an offence under the Perjury Act 1911`
    `sch 3 para 2 an offence under section 89 of the Criminal Justice Act 1967`
    `sch 3 para 3 an offence under section 20BB of the Taxes Management Act 1970`
    `sch 3 para 4 an offence under section 11 of the European Communities Act 1972`
    `sch 3 para 5 an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979`
    `sch 3 para 6 an offence under the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979`
    `sch 3 para 7 an offence under the Estate Agency Act 1979, or specified for the purposes of section 3 of that Act in the Estate Agents (Specified Offences) (No 2) Order 1991`
    `sch 3 para 8 an offence under any of sections 1 to 5 of the Forgery and Counterfeiting Act 1981`
    `sch 3 para 9 an offence under section 35 of the Administration of Justice Act 1985`
    `sch 3 para 10 an offence under section 11(1) or 13 of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986`
    `sch 3 para 11 an offence under section 1, 2, 3, 3ZA or 3A of the Computer Misuse Act 1990`
    `sch 3 para 12 an offence under section 112 or 114 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992`
    `sch 3 para 13 an offence under section 52 of the Criminal Justice Act 1993`
    `sch 3 para 14 an offence under the Value Added Tax Act 1994`
    `sch 3 para 15 an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995`
    `sch 3 para 16 an offence under the Data Protection Act 1998`
    `sch 3 para 17 an offence under the Terrorism Act 2000`
    `sch 3 para 18 an offence under paragraph 7(2) or (3) of Schedule 3 to the Anti-Terrorism, Crime and Security Act 2001`
    `sch 3 para 19 an offence under the Money Laundering Regulations 2001, 2003 or 2007 or under these Regulations`
    `sch 3 para 20 an offence under section 35 of the Tax Credits Act 2002`
    `sch 3 para 21 an offence under Part 7 or Part 8 of, or listed in Schedule 2, 4 or 5 to, the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`
    `sch 3 para 22 an offence under the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005`
    `sch 3 para 23 an offence under the Terrorism Act 2006`
    `sch 3 para 24 an offence under section 1, 2, 6 or 7 of the Bribery Act 2010`
    `sch 3 para 25 an offence under section 45 of the Serious Crime Act 2015`
    `sch 3 para 26 an offence under Parts 1, 2, 3, 5, 6 or 7 of the Investigatory Powers Act 2016`
    `sch 3 para 27 an offence under section 45 or 46 of the Criminal Finances Act 2017`
    `sch 3 para 28 an offence under the Data Protection Act 2018, apart from an offence under section 173 of that Act`
    `sch 3 para 28 exclusion an offence under section 173 of the Data Protection Act 2018`
    `sch 3 para 29 an offence of cheating the public revenue`
    `sch 3 para 30 an offence under the law of any part of the United Kingdom consisting of being knowingly concerned in the fraudulent evasion of tax`
    `sch 3 para 31 any offence which has deception or dishonesty as one of its components`
    `sch 3 para 32 the common law offences of conspiracy to defraud and perverting the course of justice`
    `sch 3 para 33 an offence of attempting, conspiring or inciting the commission of an offence specified in this Schedule`
    `sch 3 para 34 an offence under section 44 of the Serious Crime Act 2007`
    `sch 3 para 35 an offence of aiding, abetting, counselling or procuring the commission of an offence specified in this Schedule`
    `sch 3 para 36 an act done outside the United Kingdom that is an offence abroad`
    `sch 3 none of these paragraphs`

-- Schedule 3 para 36: an act which constituted an offence under the law of a foreign country and would have constituted an offence under any of paragraphs 1 to 34 if it had been done in a part of the United Kingdom, by a person linked to a part of it, or as regards the United Kingdom.  "Paragraphs 1 to 34" is applied literally: paragraph 35 (aiding and abetting) is not in the range.
-- src:3035 | An act which—
-- src:3036 | (a) constituted an offence under the law of a foreign country, and
-- src:3037 | (b) would have constituted an offence under any of paragraphs 1 to 34 under the law of any part of the United Kingdom if it had been done—
-- src:3038 | (i) in that part of the United Kingdom;
-- src:3039 | (ii) by a person who is linked to part of the United Kingdom (within the meaning of paragraph 5(3) of Schedule 7A to the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (connection with relevant part of the United Kingdom) ); or
-- src:3040 | (iii) as regards the United Kingdom.
@ref sch 3 para 36 (src:3035-3040)
GIVEN `the act constituted an offence under the law of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the paragraph, from 1 to 36, under which the act would have been an offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done in a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done by a person linked to a part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done as regards the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 3 para 36 the act is a relevant offence` IS
    IF NOT `the act constituted an offence under the law of a foreign country`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An act which— (a) constituted an offence under the law of a foreign country"
    ELSE IF     `the number of the paragraph, from 1 to 36, under which the act would have been an offence` >= 1
            AND `the number of the paragraph, from 1 to 36, under which the act would have been an offence` <= 34
            AND (   `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done in a part of the United Kingdom`
                 OR `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done by a person linked to a part of the United Kingdom`
                 OR `the act would have constituted that offence if it had been done as regards the United Kingdom`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would have constituted an offence under any of paragraphs 1 to 34"; paragraph 35 and paragraph 36 itself are outside that range, and so is an act that would not have been an offence in any of the three settings

-- Schedule 3 as a whole (seam S-5, answering): is the offence a relevant offence?  An offence in one of paragraphs 1 to 35 is, except that paragraph 28 says "apart from an offence under section 173" of the Data Protection Act 2018: an offence the caller places in that exclusion answers JUST FALSE (it is not in paragraph 28; if another paragraph catches it, name that paragraph).  An offence in none of the paragraphs is not shown to be one: regulation 26(14) says that "the offences listed in Schedule 3 are relevant offences" and does not say others are not (the term is otherwise undefined).
