-- SEAM S-5 (answering)
@ref sch 3 (src:3000-3040)
GIVEN `which paragraph of Schedule 3 the offence falls within` IS A `sch 3 paragraph`
      `sch 3 para 36 the act is a relevant offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence` IS
    CONSIDER `which paragraph of Schedule 3 the offence falls within`
    WHEN `sch 3 para 36 an act done outside the United Kingdom that is an offence abroad` THEN `sch 3 para 36 the act is a relevant offence`
    WHEN `sch 3 none of these paragraphs` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the Schedule lists offences and nothing says that an offence outside the list is not a relevant offence
    WHEN `sch 3 para 28 exclusion an offence under section 173 of the Data Protection Act 2018` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offence under the Data Protection Act 2018, apart from an offence under section 173 of that Act" [marginal (a)]
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Schedule 3AZA -- Material discrepancies`

-- Schedule 3AZA para 1: where a material discrepancy may arise.  The rendering prints the Schedule's lines without paragraph numbers.  The Schedule refers to "the condition in paragraph 2" (line 3043) and "a form listed in paragraph 3", and the lines that state those are 3044 and 3047, so lines 3042-3043 are read together as paragraph 1 (fork F-3AZA-NUMBERS).
-- src:3042 | A material discrepancy in this Schedule may arise, as the case may be, in relation to information about a beneficial owner within the meaning of regulation 3 of these Regulations (including about a person of significant control within the meaning of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006) and in relation to information about a registrable beneficial owner within the meaning of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022.
-- src:3043 | A material discrepancy in this Schedule is one which satisfies the condition in paragraph 2, including one which is in a form listed in paragraph 3.
@ref sch 3AZA para 1 (src:3042-3043)
-- SEAM S-K2 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 5 and 6 the individual is a beneficial owner of the customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information is about a person of significant control within the meaning of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is about a registrable beneficial owner within the meaning of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 3AZA para 1 a material discrepancy may arise in relation to the information` IS
    IF (`reg 5 and 6 the individual is a beneficial owner of the customer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the information is about a person of significant control within the meaning of Part 21A of the Companies Act 2006` OR `the information is about a registrable beneficial owner within the meaning of Part 3 of Schedule 1 to the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may arise, as the case may be, in relation to information about a beneficial owner ... and in relation to information about a registrable beneficial owner"

-- Schedule 3AZA para 2: the condition.  "May reasonably be considered" is a judgment the text hands to whoever considers it; it is taken as a plain input for each limb.
-- src:3044 | The condition in this paragraph is that the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered—
-- src:3045 | (a) to be linked to money laundering or terrorist financing; or
-- src:3046 | (b) to conceal details of the business of the customer.
@ref sch 3AZA para 2 (src:3044-3046)
GIVEN `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to be linked to money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to conceal details of the business of the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 3AZA para 2 the discrepancy satisfies the condition` IS
    IF `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to be linked to money laundering or terrorist financing` OR `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to conceal details of the business of the customer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to be linked to money laundering or terrorist financing` OR `the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered to conceal details of the business of the customer`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer that another provision gives is not in
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The condition in this paragraph is that the discrepancy, by its nature, and having regard to all the circumstances, may reasonably be considered— (a) to be linked to money laundering or terrorist financing; or (b) to conceal details of the business of the customer" [marginal (a)]

-- Schedule 3AZA para 3: the forms of discrepancy that are listed.
-- src:3047 | Discrepancies listed in this paragraph are in the form of—
-- src:3048 | (a) a difference in name;
-- src:3049 | (b) an incorrect entry for nature of control;
-- src:3050 | (c) an incorrect entry for date of birth;
-- src:3051 | (d) an incorrect entry for nationality;
-- src:3052 | (e) an incorrect entry for correspondence address;
-- src:3053 | (f) a missing entry for a person of significant control or a registrable beneficial owner;
-- src:3054 | (g) an incorrect entry for the date the individual became a registrable person.
@ref sch 3AZA para 3 (src:3047-3054)
DECLARE `sch 3AZA para 3 form` IS ONE OF
    `sch 3AZA para 3(a) a difference in name`
    `sch 3AZA para 3(b) an incorrect entry for nature of control`
    `sch 3AZA para 3(c) an incorrect entry for date of birth`
    `sch 3AZA para 3(d) an incorrect entry for nationality`
    `sch 3AZA para 3(e) an incorrect entry for correspondence address`
    `sch 3AZA para 3(f) a missing entry for a person of significant control or a registrable beneficial owner`
    `sch 3AZA para 3(g) an incorrect entry for the date the individual became a registrable person`
    `sch 3AZA para 3 some other form`

@ref sch 3AZA para 3 (src:3047-3054)
GIVEN form IS A `sch 3AZA para 3 form`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 3AZA para 3 the discrepancy is in a form listed in paragraph 3` IS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `sch 3AZA para 3(a) a difference in name` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3AZA para 3(b) an incorrect entry for nature of control` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3AZA para 3(c) an incorrect entry for date of birth` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3AZA para 3(d) an incorrect entry for nationality` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3AZA para 3(e) an incorrect entry for correspondence address` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3AZA para 3(f) a missing entry for a person of significant control or a registrable beneficial owner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3AZA para 3(g) an incorrect entry for the date the individual became a registrable person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3AZA para 3 some other form` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Discrepancies listed in this paragraph are in the form of—" the seven forms; a form not among them is not listed in the paragraph [marginal (a)]

-- Schedule 3AZA as a whole (seam S-6, answering): is the discrepancy a material discrepancy?  The condition in paragraph 2 makes it one.  A listed form that does not meet the condition is neither said to be material nor said not to be: "including" leaves it open (fork F-3AZA-INCLUDING).  Neither the condition nor a listed form: the Schedule's "is one which satisfies the condition" is read as closing the definition.
-- src:3043 | A material discrepancy in this Schedule is one which satisfies the condition in paragraph 2, including one which is in a form listed in paragraph 3.
-- SEAM S-6 (answering)
@ref sch 3AZA (src:3043)
GIVEN `sch 3AZA para 1 a material discrepancy may arise in relation to the information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3AZA para 2 the discrepancy satisfies the condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3AZA para 3 the discrepancy is in a form listed in paragraph 3` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sch 3AZA the discrepancy is a material discrepancy` IS
    IF NOT (`sch 3AZA para 1 a material discrepancy may arise in relation to the information` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A material discrepancy in this Schedule may arise, as the case may be, in relation to information about a beneficial owner ..."
    ELSE IF `sch 3AZA para 2 the discrepancy satisfies the condition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `sch 3AZA para 3 the discrepancy is in a form listed in paragraph 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including one which is in a form listed in paragraph 3" does not say that a listed form which fails the condition is material, or that it is not
              ELSE IF `sch 3AZA para 2 the discrepancy satisfies the condition` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A material discrepancy in this Schedule is one which satisfies the condition in paragraph 2" [marginal (a)]
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the condition in paragraph 2 has not been answered
